{"availability":"available","full":"FlowLLM-AI/AxonX","name":"AxonX","description":"Agent-native quantitative research harness. Help agents develop and improve research plugins, run experiments, and analyze traceable results through CLI, MCP, and Studio.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":5,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-04T14:26:42Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:17:13Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://flowllm-ai.github.io/AxonX/","topics":["agent-harness","ai-agents","backtesting","factor-research","mcp","plugins","qlib","quantitative-finance","quantitative-research"],"demo":"https://flowllm-ai.github.io/AxonX/playground/?lang=en","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.660Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.660Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.660Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.660Z","stars":5,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Turn research prompts into quantitative code and traceable experiments.","AxonX is an agent-native harness for quantitative research, providing unified tools and a runtime for quantitative code development, experiment execution, and result analysis.","Combine your exploration prompt with the AxonX Skill, and use an external or built-in Agent to develop a new research plugin or optimize an existing one. The Agent writes quantitative code, runs experiments through AxonX, inspects results, and iterates on factors, models, and portfolio strategies. You define the research question; the Agent implements it; the Harness manages execution and evidence."],"features":["Turn research questions into quantitative code. The Skill teaches plugin authoring, Task contracts, execution, and evidence inspection; your prompt defines what the Agent explores. → AxonX Skill","Build on Qlib’s Alpha158 baseline. Add features, change training logic, or develop portfolio policies in plugins while reusing compatible implementations and artifacts. → Alpha158 · Factor · Strategy","Execute experiments with consistent contracts. Discover typed inputs and outputs, submit worker-process Tasks, follow progress and logs, wait for completion, or cancel a run. → Task management","Connect code changes to evidence. Inspect configurations, Task/Run IDs, dependencies, models, predictions, and backtest artifacts to investigate failures and compare candidates. → Task lineage · Experiment design","Use your preferred Agent and execution target. Work through an external Agent or Studio's built-in Agent, inspect results visually, and run Tasks on a selected local or remote service. → Agent integration · Remote…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FlowLLM-AI/AxonX/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4a73e204dd7f38f709d29e64baddd5af669175abdd8db0ddb4d74b37f897906c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:39.865Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.753Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Turn research prompts into quantitative code and traceable experiments.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FlowLLM-AI/AxonX/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4a73e204dd7f38f709d29e64baddd5af669175abdd8db0ddb4d74b37f897906c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FlowLLM-AI/AxonX/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.753Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T07:17:13Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FlowLLM-AI/AxonX/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:41.754Z","hash":"4a73e204dd7f38f709d29e64baddd5af669175abdd8db0ddb4d74b37f897906c","originalBytes":21519,"storedBytes":21519,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["axonx","docs","research","agent","plugins","qlib","plugin","service","task","alpha158","factor","target","code","execution","see","strategy","studio","development","remote","token","cli","install","run","data","local","model","quantitative","training","a158","baseline","built-in","experiment","installatio